  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.3: Five fixes targeting live-preview consumers of the Avalonia renderer and the PDF table layout. AvaloniaRenderer now emits `DocumentLayout.Title` (#15), weights table star columns by content so wide tables fit their viewport instead of overflowing horizontally (#16), and accepts a `WrapInScrollViewer` opt-out so hosts that already provide a scroll container don't have to unwrap the result (#18). `BlockLayout` now carries the originating AST node's `SourceRange`, enabling editor sync-scroll without walking the AST in parallel (#19). The PDF renderer allocates auto-sized table column widths by natural content width instead of the longest-word minimum, so prose columns no longer collapse to one-word-per-line (#17). See CHANGELOG.md.",
